WEBVTT

00:04.001 --> 00:05.211
THUNDER GATE

00:05.294 --> 00:07.922
FIVE YEARS AGO

00:10.007 --> 00:12.384
[people clamoring]

00:12.468 --> 00:14.386
SEPTEMBER 12, 2034
TEN YEARS SINCE THE CALAMITY

00:15.638 --> 00:16.972
[Kiruko] <i>Five years ago,</i>

00:17.056 --> 00:20.059
<i>we made our living
in the Electro-Kart Racing industry.</i>

00:20.142 --> 00:21.352
TEAM FUNAYAMA - KIRIKO TAKEHAYA

00:21.435 --> 00:23.020
Come on, Ozaki!

00:23.103 --> 00:26.023
-[engines whirring]
-[spectator] Katayama!

00:26.106 --> 00:28.442
[spectator 2] Kiriko!

00:35.282 --> 00:37.284
[both panting]

00:38.118 --> 00:40.037
-Come back!
-Stop there!

00:41.372 --> 00:42.581
[bangs]

00:43.332 --> 00:44.500
Takehaya?

00:46.252 --> 00:47.670
Damn it.

00:47.753 --> 00:50.881
-[panting]
-Don't chase them too far! Haruki!

00:59.598 --> 01:00.891
-[blow lands]
-[gasps]

01:00.975 --> 01:03.811
[panting]

01:03.894 --> 01:05.854
Let's get the hell outta here.

01:06.355 --> 01:08.983
But that little brat has seen our faces.

01:15.531 --> 01:16.365
What?

01:20.828 --> 01:24.707
Looks like you've been looking after
our young lad, huh?

01:24.790 --> 01:28.252
Robin!
These guys have been making fake tickets!

01:30.796 --> 01:32.631
[whimpers]

01:32.715 --> 01:34.925
[shrieks]

02:10.627 --> 02:12.129
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO

02:12.963 --> 02:14.173
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO

03:04.973 --> 03:06.934
[groans]

03:07.017 --> 03:11.522
Did you think you could kill me
with a tiny scrap of metal?

03:14.441 --> 03:18.654
Haruki, when you fight your enemies,
you don't need to stare into their eyes.

03:19.446 --> 03:21.240
Glaring is just something cowards do

03:21.323 --> 03:24.952
when they want to get away
with only intimidating their opponents.

03:26.370 --> 03:28.956
Avoid the eyes,
and concentrate on the collar instead.

03:29.623 --> 03:33.460
Then focus on the ground,
check how it feels beneath your feet.

03:36.130 --> 03:39.383
Those who do nothing
but look at their opponents, lose.

03:40.426 --> 03:42.511
Let's hand these guys over to the boss.

03:43.053 --> 03:45.431
Nice going, Haruki.

03:46.014 --> 03:47.683
If you want something, just ask me.

03:48.183 --> 03:49.268
[gasps]

03:53.647 --> 03:54.648
[Haruki] We're back!

03:55.441 --> 03:56.525
What meat is that?

03:56.608 --> 03:59.778
[friend] Monkey, crow and mouse. I think.

04:01.238 --> 04:04.408
Wow, cool jacket!

04:04.491 --> 04:05.701
Robin gave it to me.

04:05.784 --> 04:07.619
[chuckles] It's a little baggy.

04:08.120 --> 04:09.997
He'll grow into it quickly, though!

04:10.080 --> 04:13.667
Now I want something too.

04:13.750 --> 04:17.087
How about trousers?
Bet they'll fit if you cut them in half.

04:17.171 --> 04:19.965
[stammers] My legs are not that short!

04:20.048 --> 04:21.675
[all laugh]

04:21.758 --> 04:22.968
I'm hungry.

04:23.802 --> 04:25.137
Sis, you're back!

04:26.221 --> 04:27.347
Where did you finish?

04:27.431 --> 04:30.309
Didn't you see? I was disqualified.
I fell out of my kart.

04:30.392 --> 04:32.269
What? Did you hurt yourself?

04:32.769 --> 04:34.980
No, I'm okay.
The other drivers went around me.

04:35.689 --> 04:36.940
Right, Doc?

04:37.024 --> 04:39.401
That's so dangerous.
You gotta be more careful!

04:39.902 --> 04:41.945
You really should drive more safely.

04:42.529 --> 04:43.530
I get it, I get it.

04:43.614 --> 04:44.948
REPORTS OF SPECTATORS
GOING MISSING

04:45.032 --> 04:47.284
Oh, yeah, Kiriko.

04:49.578 --> 04:52.206
I attached a flash to my camera.

04:52.289 --> 04:54.583
Let's take some new photos to sell.
[giggles]

04:55.167 --> 04:57.419
Take one of me and Doc, then.

04:57.503 --> 04:58.837
I'm good, thanks.

04:58.921 --> 05:00.005
Ready!

05:03.383 --> 05:04.968
-Time to go.
-Okay.

05:05.552 --> 05:06.678
[Kiriko] Thanks, Doc.

05:07.179 --> 05:11.308
Haruki, I heard the doc
is researching "Man-eaters,"

05:11.391 --> 05:13.560
and even experimenting on humans.

05:13.644 --> 05:14.770
What?

05:14.853 --> 05:16.772
[friend 2]
Robin's investigating at the moment.

05:17.314 --> 05:20.108
But it'd be better if Kiriko
didn't get too close to him.

05:20.776 --> 05:21.777
[huffs]

05:25.822 --> 05:27.741
CURRENTLY IN USE
BY FUNAYAMA ORPHANAGE

05:27.824 --> 05:30.744
KIRIKO AND HARUKI TAKEHAYA

05:31.537 --> 05:33.497
[Kiriko] Haruki, aren't you cold?

05:34.081 --> 05:36.375
No, you?

05:36.458 --> 05:37.501
Freezing.

05:37.584 --> 05:40.003
Eh. Wanna get in here?

05:42.756 --> 05:44.716
You're actually getting in?

05:44.800 --> 05:46.093
[distant footsteps]

05:48.720 --> 05:49.721
What's happening?

05:50.222 --> 05:52.224
There's a Man-eater in the third district!

05:52.307 --> 05:54.726
It's not coming this way,
so go back to sleep.

05:55.727 --> 05:57.437
-Let's go, Robin!
-Coming!

06:00.816 --> 06:01.984
Are you going?

06:02.067 --> 06:05.320
It's okay, I have the gun that I made,

06:06.446 --> 06:08.282
and I want to be helpful to Robin.

06:08.365 --> 06:09.783
[exhales]

06:14.162 --> 06:17.249
[Kiruko] <i>If I think about those days…</i>

06:19.293 --> 06:20.961
<i>they seem like heaven to me now.</i>

06:21.044 --> 06:22.129
KIRIKO AND HARUKI

06:23.505 --> 06:24.965
[crossbow shoots]

06:25.507 --> 06:26.842
[person] Not bad.

06:27.467 --> 06:30.679
You killed a Man-eater
with that weapon last week?

06:31.305 --> 06:32.306
Yeah.

06:32.889 --> 06:36.768
I'm not playing around!
I told you not to come. It's dangerous!

06:37.811 --> 06:39.313
I made Robin angry, though.

06:41.356 --> 06:44.192
-Ten years ago, Robin had a sister my age.
-[children laughing]

06:44.276 --> 06:46.945
He lost her in the Great Disaster.

06:47.613 --> 06:51.783
Since then, he's been overprotective.

06:53.285 --> 06:55.537
Wait! What time is it?

06:55.621 --> 06:59.791
Uh, which watch is right again?

07:00.667 --> 07:02.711
-That one.
-Twenty after two.

07:02.794 --> 07:05.714
I have to go! Sis's race starts at three!

07:05.797 --> 07:06.798
See you later!

07:07.299 --> 07:09.468
[person] Robin might be overprotective,

07:10.052 --> 07:11.803
but that guy is obsessed with his sister.

07:12.304 --> 07:13.388
Right?

07:14.014 --> 07:15.932
SEPTEMBER 20, 2034
TEN YEARS SINCE THE CALAMITY

07:18.268 --> 07:20.270
[engines revving, whirring]

07:28.945 --> 07:30.822
[Haruki] Okay, just made it.

07:31.490 --> 07:33.241
[distant crash]

07:33.742 --> 07:34.743
Mmm.

07:46.213 --> 07:47.964
[thud]

07:52.177 --> 07:54.221
[gasps] Help!

07:54.304 --> 07:57.391
There's a Man-eater
at the end of the track!

07:57.474 --> 07:59.851
It can turn invisible,
same as the one before!

07:59.935 --> 08:03.355
[spectators clamoring]

08:03.438 --> 08:05.023
[spectators cheering]

08:05.107 --> 08:07.901
[commentator] <i>All karts are off at once!</i>

08:07.984 --> 08:10.904
<i>What kind of race will it be today?</i>

08:10.987 --> 08:11.988
Sis.

08:14.116 --> 08:16.618
[panting] <i>The Man-eater's gone
into the arcade.</i>

08:16.702 --> 08:19.329
<i>It's probably seven or eight minutes
until the karts get there.</i>

08:20.956 --> 08:22.124
<i>I'll drive it away.</i>

08:24.751 --> 08:26.044
<i>I know I can do it.</i>

08:29.005 --> 08:30.507
[commentator] <i>After the long straight,</i>

08:30.590 --> 08:33.593
<i>karts eight, three and four
round the second corner.</i>

08:34.261 --> 08:37.389
<i>It's a crash for two and five,
a spin that will set them way back!</i>

08:37.472 --> 08:39.766
The rest are off towards Sensoji.

08:39.850 --> 08:42.269
<i>Number four, Takehaya,
you pulled that off well!</i>

08:42.352 --> 08:44.271
-Goddamn it!
-Nice one, Kiriko!

08:47.941 --> 08:48.942
[Haruki] <i>Where is it?</i>

08:49.735 --> 08:51.194
<i>Has it left the course?</i>

08:53.029 --> 08:54.114
Got it!

08:59.953 --> 09:01.580
[clanging]

09:02.205 --> 09:04.583
<i>Unbelievable, it barely hurt it.</i>

09:05.917 --> 09:07.210
[Man-eater rumbles]

09:15.886 --> 09:16.928
[groans]

09:19.973 --> 09:23.143
[breathes shakily]

09:30.317 --> 09:31.318
[grunts]

09:33.487 --> 09:35.322
[Man-eater groans]

09:35.947 --> 09:38.033
Finally, got a hit. Whoa!

09:39.326 --> 09:40.911
[grunting]

09:42.954 --> 09:44.206
My arm!

09:44.289 --> 09:45.791
[grunting]

09:45.874 --> 09:47.459
Let me go!

09:49.044 --> 09:50.462
[screams]

09:51.546 --> 09:53.799
[whimpers]

09:54.299 --> 09:55.759
<i>It's eating me.</i>

09:55.842 --> 09:57.511
[screams]

09:57.594 --> 09:59.513
Robin, help me!

09:59.596 --> 10:01.431
[commentator] <i>Takehaya's in the lead,</i>

10:01.515 --> 10:03.725
<i>exiting the third corner
towards the arcade.</i>

10:04.309 --> 10:07.562
<i>They'll be momentarily out of sight.</i>

10:07.646 --> 10:09.064
<i>The Asakusa Race Association</i>

10:09.147 --> 10:12.609
<i>is in the process of arranging for cameras
to be installed throughout the course.</i>

10:12.692 --> 10:15.862
<i>If you can offer such a service,
then by all means, please get in touch.</i>

10:15.946 --> 10:19.908
Stop! There's a Man-eater!
Call the race off!

10:19.991 --> 10:21.618
Go back and tell the headquarters.

10:21.701 --> 10:22.702
Okay.

10:24.913 --> 10:27.040
[ripping, squelching]

10:27.123 --> 10:29.334
[squelching continues]

10:29.417 --> 10:30.460
[Kiriko gasps]

10:36.633 --> 10:38.051
[gasps]

10:38.134 --> 10:39.135
Haruki?

10:43.723 --> 10:45.141
Haruki!

10:52.607 --> 10:55.110
-[Man-eater rumbles]
-[groans]

10:55.944 --> 10:56.945
Give him back.

10:57.821 --> 11:00.991
Let him go!

11:02.576 --> 11:04.578
[panting]

11:09.541 --> 11:10.709
[gasps]

11:12.085 --> 11:14.754
[crying] Haru… No.

11:15.964 --> 11:16.965
It can't be.

11:17.591 --> 11:19.009
[sobs]

11:23.513 --> 11:26.391
Somebody! Anybody, quickly!

11:26.892 --> 11:29.144
Help!

11:30.145 --> 11:32.856
[Haruki] <i>Sis…</i>

11:35.108 --> 11:36.985
<i>She's so close.</i>

11:39.362 --> 11:41.364
<i>Sis…</i>

11:42.866 --> 11:44.534
[gunshot]

12:40.799 --> 12:42.717
CURRENTLY IN USE
BY FUNAYAMA ORPHANAGE

12:44.052 --> 12:45.095
[Haruki] <i>Everyone…</i>

12:50.225 --> 12:51.309
<i>Sis?</i>

12:57.774 --> 12:59.025
<i>My head…</i>

13:00.235 --> 13:01.277
<i>It's so hot.</i>

13:05.281 --> 13:08.785
<i>Sis.</i>

13:18.586 --> 13:20.588
[gunshot]

13:37.063 --> 13:38.106
[echoing] Sis?

13:38.606 --> 13:39.607
[strains]

13:42.235 --> 13:44.279
[shrieks]

13:44.362 --> 13:45.488
Sis!

13:46.281 --> 13:47.907
[gasping]

13:53.997 --> 13:56.249
Takehaya has regained consciousness!

14:15.810 --> 14:18.188
[patient] Apparently,
there's another Man-eater in the area,

14:18.772 --> 14:20.857
and a child is dead.

14:21.357 --> 14:22.525
That's horrifying.

14:22.609 --> 14:23.777
Excuse me.

14:27.530 --> 14:28.656
Why…

14:34.746 --> 14:37.540
Si-- Sis?

14:37.624 --> 14:39.209
[gasps, pants]

14:41.377 --> 14:42.378
Me?

14:42.462 --> 14:44.089
-[nurse] The patient, she--
-[Haruki screams]

14:46.007 --> 14:47.050
Takehaya!

14:47.634 --> 14:49.177
You shouldn't be walking yet!

14:49.260 --> 14:51.471
[shrieks] Stop! I'm Haruki!

14:52.055 --> 14:53.348
-Where's Sis?
-Get a tranquilizer!

14:53.431 --> 14:55.433
-[nurse 2] Going!
-[Haruki] I want my sister! S-Sis!

14:55.517 --> 14:58.728
-[nurse 3] You need to calm down.
-[Haruki] Sis! Sis!

15:05.610 --> 15:09.197
[nurse] I think that
the shock of her brother's death

15:09.280 --> 15:11.991
has led her to believe
that she is her brother.

15:12.617 --> 15:13.743
The poor girl.

15:14.786 --> 15:16.496
-[Haruki] The doctor.
-Hmm?

15:17.455 --> 15:19.290
What did the doctor do?

15:19.916 --> 15:21.126
He must know what happened.

15:21.709 --> 15:22.794
Where's the doctor?

15:23.461 --> 15:27.757
After giving you both medical attention,
the doctor left town.

15:27.841 --> 15:28.967
[gasps]

15:29.050 --> 15:33.471
You were both brought here
on the verge of death.

15:33.555 --> 15:35.807
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

15:35.890 --> 15:38.268
What happened to your brother
is incredibly upsetting,

15:39.018 --> 15:41.187
but no matter what treatment we used,

15:41.271 --> 15:44.899
without the doctor,
I believe you would both be dead.

15:45.692 --> 15:47.735
--SOJI HOSPITAL

15:47.819 --> 15:48.945
[Haruki] <i>I don't understand.</i>

15:50.405 --> 15:52.365
<i>Last time I saw her,</i>

15:53.658 --> 15:56.661
<i>she was crying, but definitely alive.</i>

15:58.163 --> 16:02.625
<i>Was she eaten by the Man-eater?</i>

16:04.169 --> 16:05.587
<i>One thing is undeniable.</i>

16:06.254 --> 16:08.339
<i>I am definitely still Haruki.</i>

16:09.215 --> 16:10.508
<i>The proof of that</i>

16:11.217 --> 16:15.013
<i>is the sorrow splintering through me
at the news of my sister's death,</i>

16:15.597 --> 16:18.933
<i>and the occasional faint solace</i>

16:19.559 --> 16:24.022
<i>of having inherited
the body of someone I love.</i>

16:25.523 --> 16:30.528
<i>By the time my sister's wounds had healed,
and I could start to move her body again,</i>

16:31.196 --> 16:33.531
<i>nearly four months had passed.</i>

16:38.077 --> 16:41.039
<i>Robin must be investigating
what that doctor was up to.</i>

16:41.789 --> 16:43.791
<i>I'm sure he will be able to figure it out.</i>

16:44.292 --> 16:46.628
<i>He'll be able to tell me
why I have become my sister,</i>

16:47.378 --> 16:48.880
<i>and why she had to die.</i>

16:48.963 --> 16:50.131
ASAKUSA RACE ASSOCIATION
HEADQUARTERS

16:50.882 --> 16:52.675
-[Haruki] Excuse me.
-Huh?

16:53.259 --> 16:56.554
I'm hoping to see Robin Inazaki
from the Asakusa Race Association--

16:56.638 --> 16:59.432
Ah, that's not possible.

17:01.226 --> 17:03.811
Sometime around September last year,

17:05.146 --> 17:07.106
I'm pretty sure he was murdered.

17:09.192 --> 17:11.903
<i>There was an increase in disappearances
around here last year.</i>

17:12.403 --> 17:15.156
<i>Seems he got tangled up
in trying to investigate.</i>

17:15.782 --> 17:19.202
<i>Then, just like that,
he ended up disappearing too.</i>

17:19.786 --> 17:22.205
[panting, gulps]

17:23.206 --> 17:25.291
[Haruki] Ken! Ran!

17:25.792 --> 17:26.834
Director!

17:27.502 --> 17:28.795
Anyone!

17:33.466 --> 17:34.592
[gasps]

17:34.676 --> 17:38.429
Please! W-What happened to
the orphanage that was here?

17:39.055 --> 17:41.599
-It was moved elsewhere.
-What?

17:42.183 --> 17:44.894
[person] Their highest earning racer died…

17:44.978 --> 17:46.396
REPORTS OF SPECTATORS
GOING MISSING

17:46.479 --> 17:48.523
…and the leader went missing.

17:48.606 --> 17:53.069
I expect with all the bad luck,
they gave up on this town.

17:56.197 --> 17:58.199
[door opens, creaks]

18:01.077 --> 18:02.078
[door closes]

18:13.089 --> 18:14.132
[Haruki] Sis.

18:15.717 --> 18:17.969
Robin. [sobs]

18:21.472 --> 18:24.934
[employee] <i>Then, just like that,
he ended up disappearing too.</i>

18:25.018 --> 18:27.729
[person] <i>The leader went missing.</i>

18:27.812 --> 18:30.773
[gasps] "Missing"?

18:30.857 --> 18:32.066
"Disappeared"?

18:32.650 --> 18:35.445
There isn't actually any proof
that Robin is dead.

18:39.449 --> 18:41.451
There's no way Robin can be dead.

18:42.744 --> 18:44.537
He must be alive somewhere.

18:46.831 --> 18:47.832
The doctor.

18:48.458 --> 18:50.335
The doctor has the answer to everything.

18:50.418 --> 18:54.213
Where Robin is, why my sister is dead…

18:54.297 --> 18:55.965
[crying]

18:56.049 --> 18:58.760
…and why I'm living inside her body!

18:59.635 --> 19:00.470
TRIP GUARD

19:00.553 --> 19:02.055
PROTECTION FROM WILD ANIMALS,
BANDITS AND MAN-EATERS - KIRUKO

19:02.722 --> 19:05.058
[Kiruko] <i>After that,
I lived in various towns,</i>

19:05.141 --> 19:06.559
<i>searching for the two of them,</i>

19:06.642 --> 19:10.521
<i>accepting requests,
and doing everything by myself.</i>

19:13.358 --> 19:17.070
Four years later, I met you in Nakano.

19:17.153 --> 19:18.154
DO NOT ENTER

19:24.786 --> 19:27.413
It's the first time I've told anyone that.

19:29.332 --> 19:31.250
I want to check something with you.

19:32.418 --> 19:35.588
Would it be better
if I stopped calling you "Sis"?

19:35.671 --> 19:36.923
That?

19:37.006 --> 19:38.591
Ah, don't worry about it.

19:38.674 --> 19:42.303
You've been calling me that for a month,
pretty sure we're both used to it now.

19:42.929 --> 19:47.183
Well, there you go.
You'll have to think of me as a man now.

19:47.266 --> 19:49.644
I can't wrap my mind around it
just like that!

19:54.107 --> 19:56.859
Anyway,
you're getting pretty good looking.

19:56.943 --> 19:59.112
I'm sure you'll meet someone
more appropriate soon.

19:59.195 --> 20:02.490
I won't find a girl
I get along with this well.

20:02.573 --> 20:04.992
That's because we're both guys.

20:06.327 --> 20:09.539
[Maru] So the photo
of Jane Inamura, right?

20:09.622 --> 20:10.998
It's Robin Inazaki.

20:12.083 --> 20:14.210
[Maru] What do you think about him?

20:16.254 --> 20:17.588
Well,

20:18.214 --> 20:21.467
we grew up in the same house,
so I guess he's like family.

20:21.968 --> 20:23.511
But he's also a close friend.

20:24.470 --> 20:26.013
I suppose I admire him.

20:26.097 --> 20:27.515
[Maru groans]

20:28.099 --> 20:30.059
Because we're both guys! I look up to him.

20:30.143 --> 20:31.936
You still don't get it, do you?

20:32.019 --> 20:35.314
What do you expect
when you tell someone something like that?

20:35.398 --> 20:36.858
[groans]

20:36.941 --> 20:39.235
Maybe a good night's sleep
will sort your head out.

20:39.735 --> 20:40.987
[Maru] Fine.

20:41.070 --> 20:43.823
Maybe when I wake up
this will all turn out to be a dream.

20:44.407 --> 20:45.908
[distant shrieking]

20:45.992 --> 20:47.785
What now? What's the racket for?

20:48.828 --> 20:50.163
What is it?

20:50.246 --> 20:52.957
There was a huge fish outside the window.

20:53.040 --> 20:54.041
A fish?

20:56.002 --> 21:00.256
The window is wet,
even though it's not raining.

21:00.840 --> 21:01.841
Strange.

21:03.009 --> 21:05.803
Maru, go and tell the captain
to keep an eye--

21:05.887 --> 21:07.555
-[rumbling]
-[both whimper]

21:08.139 --> 21:09.348
[rumbling]

21:15.271 --> 21:16.439
A Man-eater.

22:46.946 --> 22:48.948
[water bubbling]

22:50.950 --> 22:53.869
[Kuku grunting]

22:56.747 --> 22:58.291
Is it a baby?

22:58.374 --> 23:00.710
Can I have it?

23:01.210 --> 23:04.755
I promised to give this one to Tokio.
You can have the next.

23:04.839 --> 23:06.257
Sounds good to me!

23:06.340 --> 23:08.301
I like your weird drawing.

23:08.884 --> 23:09.885
You think it's weird?

23:09.969 --> 23:13.264
Obviously! Proper babies--

23:13.931 --> 23:17.351
<i>Climbing on tables is forbidden, Kuku.</i>

23:17.435 --> 23:20.354
Stop annoying Kona and come with me.

23:20.438 --> 23:21.522
Ow! Hey--

23:25.526 --> 23:28.613
If you're going to be nasty about them,
then stop asking for Kona's drawings!

23:28.696 --> 23:30.239
I was saying they were good!

23:30.823 --> 23:33.909
Besides, I've seen one. A real baby.

23:35.202 --> 23:38.623
Real babies don't have faces.

23:40.999 --> 23:42.627
<i>Want to go and see it?</i>
